; blacklisted.ini -- the servers the list will not list. Copy this file to blacklisted.ini and add lines.
; blacklisted.ini is git-ignored: it names other people's servers, so it stays on the machine that runs the list.
;
; One entry to a line. A ; or # starts a comment, so a note can follow an entry.
;
; The list reads the file when it starts and again whenever it changes: an edit takes hold within
; poll_seconds (serverlist.ini) with no restart, and a server that is on the list when an entry
; names it is taken off then. Every way of getting on is held to it: a heartbeat with or without the
; key, servers.txt and /addserver. A heartbeat from a blacklisted address is answered 403.
;
; An address: every server there, on any port.
;203.0.113.7
;
; One server: an address or a host name, and its port.
;203.0.113.7:27016
;
; A range of addresses (IPv4, CIDR).
;203.0.113.0/24
;
; A host name: the servers that name stands for. A name that resolves to a blacklisted address is refused too.
;fake.example.com
;fake.example.com:27015
